data.content:
`SafeAreaEdges="None"` only tells the page not to inset its content for safe areas — but you also need to ensure the platform actually lets your app draw behind the system bars. Common missing pieces:

**1. Hide the app-level navigation bar** (Shell or NavigationPage):
```xml
<!-- If using Shell -->
Shell.NavBarIsVisible="False"

<!-- If using NavigationPage -->
NavigationPage.HasNavigationBar="False"
```

**2. Android — enable edge-to-edge rendering:**

In `Platforms/Android/MainActivity.cs` (or via lifecycle events):
```csharp
using AndroidX.Activity;
using AndroidX.Core.View;

// In OnCreate, after base call:
EdgeToEdge.Enable(this);

// Make system bars transparent
WindowCompat.SetDecorFitsSystemWindows(Window, false);
```

Or in `MauiProgram.cs`:
```csharp
builder.ConfigureLifecycleEvents(events =>
{
    events.AddAndroid(android => android.OnCreate((activity, _) =>
    {
        EdgeToEdge.Enable((ComponentActivity)activity);
        WindowCompat.SetDecorFitsSystemWindows(activity.Window!, false);
    }));
});
```

**3. iOS — confirm safe area is disabled:**
```xml
<ContentPage xmlns:ios="clr-namespace:Microsoft.Maui.Controls.PlatformConfiguration.iOSSpecific;assembly=Microsoft.Maui.Controls"
             ios:Page.UseSafeArea="False">
```

**4. Image should fill available space:**
```xml
<Image Source="photo.jpg"
       Aspect="AspectFill"
       HorizontalOptions="Fill"
       VerticalOptions="Fill" />
```

---

**TL;DR:** `SafeAreaEdges="None"` handles the MAUI layout side, but on Android you must explicitly opt into edge-to-edge drawing with `EdgeToEdge.Enable()` + `SetDecorFitsSystemWindows(window, false)`. Also make sure Shell/NavigationPage chrome is hidden.
